A||||10||rmorgandotcom||Updating 85mph speedo to 120mph speedo.||||5||
Z||000000||rmorgandotcom||10-02-2001||11:42 PM||||How would this be done?<BR>Would I have to get a new pod?||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-02-2001||11:47 PM||||You can replace the entire pod, but that isn't necessary.<P>I'm assuming you have a V-6 Fiero.....just remove the entire pod from the dash and remove the faceplate trim.  The speedo will pop out......replce the 85MPH unit with the 120 MPH and you're done.  It is a completely bolt on thing.  You can even so this to 4-cyl Fieros, but the tach will need reworking to read correctly.<P>The best thing, in my opinion, is to replace the entire cluster (speedo, tach, fuel, temp) with those from the 120MPH car.....these gauges are backlit and will be easier to see at night.  It will also be a quicker thing......just remove the gauges from the pod and insert the new gauges and reassemble it on the dash.  It should take about an hour to an hour and a half.<P>I hope this helps.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||10-03-2001||08:31 AM||||heh the hard thing is finding 120mph speedo pods though!||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||10-03-2001||09:09 AM||||Just curious, where did you get a 120mph speedo at anyway. I've seen them go for big bux on Ebay but never saw one in person||||reg||5
Z||000004||falconhulk||10-03-2001||10:47 AM||||Since he has one post I am assuming he is new to the fiero and was asking becasue he was thinking of upgrading the speedo......not becasue he actually has one.  I would love to do this also but have not been able to find one.  I wish one of these Fiero parts places would start making them.<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||10-03-2001||11:29 AM||||I have been fortunate enough to have gotten several over the last 18 months from junk yards in my area.  It is usually the first thing to disappear from a GT when it arrives. The last one I got was last Friday and I got the entire mint condition pod with top and bottom covers for $11.  That and the $19 mint condition black dash are going into my sons 85 that we are restoring.<P>Oh, don't forget to take the odometer from the old speedo and swap it with the new one.  You wouldn't want your DMV to get you for tampering with the odometer.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gerald||10-03-2001||01:15 PM||||A friend of mine makes Lambo kit cars based on fieros. I have a nice supply of fiero parts. Including my 120 speedo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Its all free<BR>Companys name is lear 2000||||reg||1
